{
  "$schema": "../../shared/schemas/dev-workflow-rules.schema.json",
  "schema_version": 1,
  "summary": "Repo development workflow routing rules for changed files.",
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "app-subtree-local-contract",
      "summary": "App subtree changes delegate app-specific workflow details to the nearest local contract.",
      "patterns": [
        "apps/**"
      ],
      "classes": [
        "app",
        "local_contract"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "read_local_contract"
      ],
      "hot_swappable": true,
      "tcc_identity_sensitive": false,
      "commands": [],
      "verification": [],
      "notes": [
        "Repo-wide routing should not encode app-specific behavior; read the nearest subtree AGENTS.md or local playbook before choosing app tests."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "legacy-sigil-test-fixture",
      "summary": "Frozen historical Sigil payload or its bounded test-only contract changed.",
      "patterns": [
        "tests/fixtures/legacy-sigil/product/**",
        "tests/fixtures/legacy-sigil/aos-experience.fixture.json",
        "tests/legacy-sigil-fixture.test.mjs",
        "tests/schemas/aos-app-v0.test.mjs",
        "tests/schemas/aos-experience-v0.test.mjs",
        "docs/dev/test-proof-registry.d/legacy-sigil-fixture.json"
      ],
      "classes": [
        "test_fixture",
        "legacy_compatibility"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "focused_test"
      ],
      "hot_swappable": true,
      "tcc_identity_sensitive": false,
      "commands": [
        {
          "id": "legacy-sigil-fixture-contract",
          "command": "node --test tests/legacy-sigil-fixture.test.mjs tests/schemas/aos-app-v0.test.mjs tests/schemas/aos-experience-v0.test.mjs tests/active-authority-pointers.test.mjs",
          "reason": "Verify the relocated payload remains digest-sealed, test-only, schema-valid, non-discoverable, and excluded from active authority."
        }
      ],
      "verification": [],
      "notes": [
        "Static test-only route. Do not build or execute ./aos, operate the daemon, or touch TCC."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "swift-core",
      "summary": "Unified aos binary or Swift IPC sources changed.",
      "patterns": [
        "src/**/*.swift",
        "shared/swift/ipc/**/*.swift"
      ],
      "classes": [
        "swift",
        "aos_binary"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "swift_build"
      ],
      "hot_swappable": false,
      "tcc_identity_sensitive": true,
      "commands": [],
      "verification": [],
      "notes": [
        "If the repo-local ./aos binary is missing or exits 137, recover with `bash build.sh --force --no-restart` because the normal post-build verification cannot run through a broken ./aos artifact.",
        "ADR 0023 requires root build.sh with inline source fingerprinting and one plain direct swiftc link. Injected plist or metadata sections, separate linking, post-link signing, explicit identifiers, entitlements, copying, moving, binary rewriting, app wrapping, and spctl gates are prohibited.",
        "The router intentionally does not schedule the TCC-sensitive build or first launch beside ordinary checks. Finish all static commands first; then use the `aos-repo-binary-build` skill for the isolated build checkpoint.",
        "At that checkpoint, run `bash build.sh --force --no-restart`, then run `./aos help --json` as the immediately following command and stop on exit 137.",
        "After help succeeds, stop until the user manually regrants TCC and replies `finished`; then run exact `./aos ready --repair --post-permission --json` with no intervening command."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "repo-build-tooling",
      "summary": "Repo-mode build wrapper, signing, or rebuild alert behavior changed.",
      "patterns": [
        "build.sh",
        "scripts/aos-after-build",
        "scripts/aos-dev-build.mjs",
        "tests/aos-after-build.sh",
        "tests/aos-build-attestation.test.mjs",
        "tests/build-rebuild-policy.sh"
      ],
      "classes": [
        "build_tooling",
        "aos_binary"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "focused_test"
      ],
      "hot_swappable": true,
      "tcc_identity_sensitive": false,
      "commands": [
        {
          "id": "build-rebuild-policy-test",
          "command": "bash tests/build-rebuild-policy.sh",
          "reason": "Verify content-based one-link rebuilds, no post-link mutation, and the help-first launch checkpoint."
        }
      ],
      "verification": [],
      "notes": [
        "The raw recovery command for a missing or launch-killed repo ./aos is `bash build.sh --force --no-restart`; do not repair it with a separate linker or post-link mutation.",
        "After a real rebuild, ./aos help --json is the exact first launch. If it succeeds, stop for the human TCC checkpoint before any inspection or readiness command. spctl rejection is expected for the repo-local raw shape and is not an acceptance gate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "root-skill-packages",
      "summary": "Root skill package instructions or registry-backed skill contracts changed.",
      "patterns": [
        "skills/**",
        "scripts/aos-skills*.mjs",
        "tests/aos-skills-*.test.mjs"
      ],
      "classes": [
        "skills"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "skill_validation"
      ],
      "hot_swappable": true,
      "tcc_identity_sensitive": false,
      "commands": [
        {
          "id": "skills-validate",
          "command": "node scripts/aos-skills-validate.mjs --json",
          "reason": "Validate root skill package metadata, body budgets, durable backing, and install target support."
        },
        {
          "id": "skills-registry-test",
          "command": "node --test tests/aos-skills-registry.test.mjs",
          "reason": "Verify root skill registry coverage and split-skill contracts."
        }
      ],
      "verification": []
    },
    {
      "id": "pre-release-product-policy",
      "summary": "Product maturity, compatibility exception policy, or retired-skill deletion enforcement changed.",
      "patterns": [
        "AGENTS.md",
        "docs/adr/0018-installable-aos-skills.md",
        "docs/adr/0019-retire-project-agent-orchestration.md",
        "docs/adr/0039-pre-release-zero-installed-base-compatibility.md",
        "docs/dev/product-maturity.json",
        "docs/dev/residue-drift-ledger.md",
        "shared/schemas/aos-product-maturity-v0.schema.json",
        "tests/pre-release-compatibility-policy.test.mjs",
        "tests/schemas/aos-product-maturity-v0.test.mjs"
      ],
      "classes": [
        "product_policy",
        "schema"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "focused_test"
      ],
      "hot_swappable": true,
      "tcc_identity_sensitive": false,
      "commands": [
        {
          "id": "pre-release-compatibility-policy-test",
          "command": "node --test tests/pre-release-compatibility-policy.test.mjs tests/schemas/aos-product-maturity-v0.test.mjs",
          "reason": "Validate zero-installed-base facts, evidence-backed exceptions, exact active-source markers, and retired-skill absence."
        }
      ],
      "verification": [],
      "notes": [
        "Static only: scan the exact residue marker in active product/source roots and exclude archived evidence rather than grepping compatibility vocabulary broadly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "toolkit-components",
      "summary": "Reusable toolkit component or runtime browser code changed.",
      "patterns": [
        "packages/toolkit/components/**",
        "packages/toolkit/contracts/mounted-surface-menu-projection.js",
        "packages/toolkit/panel/**",
        "packages/toolkit/runtime/**",
        "packages/toolkit/status-item/**",
        "packages/toolkit/package.json",
        "packages/toolkit/package-lock.json"
      ],
      "classes": [
        "toolkit",
        "web_surface"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "component_reload",
        "focused_toolkit_test"
      ],
      "hot_swappable": true,
      "tcc_identity_sensitive": false,
      "commands": [],
      "verification": []
    },
    {
      "id": "status-item-contract",
      "summary": "Native status-item host/action admission, public toolkit, schema, or CLI transport changed.",
      "patterns": [
        "manifests/commands/source/aos/40-status-item.json",
        "manifests/commands/source/external/48-status-item.json",
        "packages/toolkit/status-item/**",
        "scripts/aos-status-item.mjs",
        "scripts/lib/status-item-output-writer.mjs",
        "shared/schemas/aos-status-item-*.schema.json",
        "shared/schemas/daemon-ipc.md",
        "shared/schemas/daemon-request.schema.json",
        "shared/schemas/daemon-response.schema.json",
        "shared/schemas/daemon-event.schema.json",
        "shared/schemas/fixtures/daemon-event/**/status-item-*.json",
        "src/commands/daemon-application-lifecycle.swift",
        "src/commands/serve.swift",
        "src/daemon/unified.swift",
        "src/display/status-item*.swift",
        "tests/daemon-ipc-schema.sh",
        "tests/fixtures/status-item-*.swift",
        "tests/status-item-contract.test.mjs"
      ],
      "classes": [
        "status_item",
        "command_contract"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "focused_test"
      ],
      "hot_swappable": true,
      "tcc_identity_sensitive": false,
      "commands": [
        {
          "id": "status-item-contract",
          "command": "node --test tests/status-item-contract.test.mjs",
          "reason": "Status-item production sources must retain original-data request validation, immutable rendered-menu identity, exact discriminated invocation and event variants, production-owned serialized admission, exhaustion parity, native/programmatic race, failed-delivery, transport, and bounded follow-stream coverage."
        },
        {
          "id": "status-item-daemon-schemas",
          "command": "bash tests/daemon-ipc-schema.sh && node --test tests/schemas/daemon-event.test.mjs",
          "reason": "Canonical request, response, invocation-result, documented dry-run, and event envelopes must retain strict status-item wire validation, exact variants, and exact error codes."
        }
      ],
      "verification": []
    },
    {
      "id": "desktop-annotation-selection",
      "summary": "Native desktop annotation selection, persistence projection, or semantic target contract changed.",
      "patterns": [
        "manifests/commands/source/aos/03-see-04-annotation.json",
        "scripts/aos-annotation-select.mjs",
        "scripts/lib/pending-annotations-model.mjs",
        "shared/schemas/aos-pending-annotation-v0.*",
        "shared/schemas/daemon-event.schema.json",
        "shared/schemas/fixtures/daemon-event/**/annotation-*.json",
        "src/daemon/annotation-selection.swift",
        "src/daemon/annotation-target-selection.swift",
        "src/perceive/ax-semantic-target.swift",
        "src/perceive/ax.swift",
        "tests/annotation-select-cli.test.mjs",
        "tests/annotation-selection-native.sh",
        "tests/lib/annotation-semantic-target-traversal-tests.swift",
        "tests/schemas/aos-pending-annotation-v0.test.mjs",
        "tests/schemas/daemon-event.test.mjs",
        "tests/toolkit/pending-annotation-model.test.mjs"
      ],
      "classes": [
        "desktop_annotation",
        "command_contract",
        "schema",
        "swift"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "focused_test",
        "schema_test"
      ],
      "hot_swappable": false,
      "tcc_identity_sensitive": true,
      "commands": [
        {
          "id": "annotation-selection-adapter",
          "command": "node --test tests/annotation-select-cli.test.mjs && bash tests/annotation-selection-native.sh",
          "reason": "Verify strict follow-stream persistence, redaction, singleton ownership, bounded geometry, semantic drill-down, and admission-only TCC checks."
        },
        {
          "id": "annotation-selection-schema",
          "command": "node --test tests/schemas/aos-pending-annotation-v0.test.mjs tests/schemas/daemon-event.test.mjs tests/toolkit/pending-annotation-model.test.mjs",
          "reason": "Verify target mode and element evidence remain closed, bounded, mode-matched, and path-free."
        },
        {
          "id": "annotation-selection-command-manifest",
          "command": "bash tests/command-manifest-generation.sh",
          "reason": "Keep geometric and semantic target form identifiers explicit in generated help."
        }
      ],
      "verification": [],
      "notes": [
        "Run these static and fake-daemon checks before the isolated repo-binary rebuild checkpoint; never use the live daemon or TCC as part of this route."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "desktop-pixel-native-baseline",
      "summary": "Foreground ScreenCaptureKit-to-Metal baseline, DesktopWorld native sheet, or explicit runtime proof command changed.",
      "patterns": [
        "src/commands/desktop-pixel-native-baseline*.swift",
        "src/display/desktop-world-native-projection*.swift",
        "src/display/desktop-world-native-sheet-geometry.swift",
        "src/display/desktop-world-native-sheet-lease.swift",
        "src/display/desktop-world-native-sheet.swift",
        "src/display/desktop-world-surface.swift",
        "src/daemon/desktop-pixel-capture-filter.swift",
        "src/daemon/desktop-pixel-native-operation.swift",
        "src/daemon/desktop-pixel-stream-lifecycle.swift",
        "src/shared/desktop-pixel-sample-admission.swift",
        "src/shared/desktop-world-display-geometry.swift",
        "src/shared/desktop-world-resource-identity.swift",
        "tests/lib/desktop-world-display-geometry-tests.swift",
        "src/main.swift"
      ],
      "classes": [
        "native_pixel_baseline",
        "swift"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "focused_test",
        "help_contract"
      ],
      "hot_swappable": false,
      "tcc_identity_sensitive": true,
      "commands": [
        {
          "id": "desktop-pixel-native-baseline-contract",
          "command": "node --test tests/desktop-pixel-native-baseline.test.mjs && bash tests/desktop-pixel-native-baseline-typecheck.sh && bash tests/command-manifest-generation.sh",
          "reason": "Keep the standalone control and AOS-owned DesktopWorld native-sheet increment daemon-free, prompt-free, in-memory, bounded, type-correct, and aligned with generated help."
        }
      ],
      "verification": [],
      "notes": [
        "The routed checks are static and typecheck-only. They do not build or execute ./aos, operate a daemon, or touch TCC.",
        "Run the native command only at a separate supervised checkpoint after the raw repo binary recovery contract is satisfied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "desktop-pixel-native-baseline-command",
      "summary": "The script-owned native baseline route, manifests, documentation, or static proofs changed.",
      "patterns": [
        "scripts/aos-runtime-desktop-pixel-baseline.mjs",
        "manifests/commands/source/aos/21-runtime.json",
        "manifests/commands/source/external/10-runtime.json",
        "docs/guides/desktop-pixel-native-baseline.md",
        "tests/desktop-pixel-native-baseline.test.mjs",
        "tests/desktop-pixel-native-baseline-typecheck.sh",
        "tests/lib/desktop-pixel-native-baseline-lifecycle-tests.swift",
        "tests/lib/desktop-pixel-metal-pipeline-tests.swift",
        "tests/lib/desktop-world-native-projection-lifecycle-tests.swift",
        "tests/lib/desktop-world-native-sheet-lease-tests.swift",
        "tests/lib/desktop-world-native-sheet-geometry-tests.swift"
      ],
      "classes": [
        "native_pixel_baseline",
        "command_contract"
      ],
      "actions": [
        "focused_test",
        "help_contract"
      ],
      "hot_swappable": true,
      "tcc_identity_sensitive": false,
      "commands": [
        {
          "id": "desktop-pixel-native-baseline-contract",
          "command": "node --test tests/desktop-pixel-native-baseline.test.mjs && bash tests/desktop-pixel-native-baseline-typecheck.sh && bash tests/command-manifest-generation.sh",
          "reason": "Keep the explicit foreground proof daemon-free, prompt-free, in-memory, bounded, type-correct, and aligned with generated help."
        }
      ],
      "verification": [],
      "notes": [
        "The routed checks are static and typecheck-only. They do not build or execute ./aos, operate a daemon, or touch TCC.",
        "Run the native command only at a separate supervised checkpoint after the raw repo binary recovery contract is satisfied."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "desktop-world-scene-engine",
      "summary": "DesktopWorld scene contracts, authoring tools, runtime session, extensions, or agent route changed.",
      "patterns": [
        "packages/toolkit/scene/**",
        "packages/toolkit/components/desktop-world-stage/**",
        "src/commands/daemon-application-lifecycle.swift",
        "src/commands/serve.swift",
        "src/daemon/desktop-world-scene-*.swift",
        "src/daemon/desktop-world-native-*.swift",
        "src/daemon/desktop-world-devtools-*.swift",
